# The failover sweep's ratchet (ADR-0055 §11): every cell of the base
# catalogue that fails today, with the decision section that owns its
# correction. A change that makes a cell pass removes its line; a new failure
# is never added without its owner. The list only shrinks.
#
# The owner is read from the finding: a second CDR where the departure sweep
# ends a call a killed primary ended behind the replication window (no marker
# tells it), §5; a final under another tag than a provisional that left inside
# the replication window, a request or final a copy sends without the record
# of what the dead owner sent, a request into a dialog the other copy ended,
# and the non-2xx a copy owes a caller the dead primary answered §4; a CSeq
# re-used outside a primary kill, §11 (no declared window covers it); a PRACK,
# an owed ACK or an in-dialog request left unanswered §2; a 2xx repeat routed
# through the other owner §8; and any other finding of a split cell §7.

